	quests: [
		{
			description: [
				"Use JEI for recipes and uses: hover an item and press R for recipes or U for uses. Search with an at-sign followed by a mod name when you only want one mod's items."
				"Use Jade to identify the block, creature or machine in front of you. Hold Create's Ponder key over Create components to watch animated explanations that are often clearer than a wall of text."
				"Use this field guide for progression, hazards and group plans. A checkmark lesson means read it, try the idea, then mark it complete; it is not pretending the game can detect good judgement."
			]
			id: "20245EF322046A0F"
			rewards: [{
				id: "08697AF894CEFF4A"
				type: "xp"
				xp: 10
			}]
			subtitle: "JEI, Jade, Ponder and the quest book answer different questions"
			tasks: [{
				id: "0C4C093B50D8C6EB"
				title: "I read this field note and tested the idea"
				type: "checkmark"
			}]
			title: "Your Four Ways to Learn"
			x: 0.0d
			y: 0.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["20245EF322046A0F"]
			description: [
				"Terralith reshapes large-scale terrain while Biomes O' Plenty adds its own plants, woods and biome palettes. TerraBlender helps biome mods cooperate, and Serene Seasons changes colour and crop behaviour over time."
				"YUNG's structures, Dungeons and Taverns, Repurposed Structures, Better Archeology and smaller landmark mods then place destinations into that terrain. Their content appears only in chunks generated with the mod installed."
				"If something seems absent, travel beyond the explored map and use Nature's Compass or Explorer's Compass selectively. A compass is a search tool, not a reason to skip every journey between discoveries."
			]
			id: "237EC65649665A03"
			rewards: [{
				id: "3415427EAFCEFF48"
				type: "xp"
				xp: 10
			}]
			subtitle: "Terrain, biomes, seasons and structures are several systems working together"
			tasks: [{
				id: "765903CC8DEE2BCB"
				title: "I read this field note and tested the idea"
				type: "checkmark"
			}]
			title: "The World Layer"
			x: 2.0d
			y: -2.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["20245EF322046A0F"]
			description: [
				"Farmer's Delight adds crops, knives, cutting boards, rich soil, stoves and multi-ingredient meals. Its Delight addons extend that pantry into the Nether, End, Aether, Twilight Forest, caves and oceans."
				"Brewin' and Chewin' handles fermentation and drinks, Herbal Brews handles tea and coffee, and Cooking for Blockheads helps arrange a practical kitchen. Serene Seasons makes crop planning matter."
				"This part of the pack is progression even when no boss bar appears. A stocked public kitchen, readable farm and guest bed can change the whole server for a new player."
				"Return here after major discoveries. The same mod may participate in several chapters: a cave ingredient can become food, a relic can change travel, and a decorative block can become the language of a whole settlement."
			]
			id: "25171C2FD0FDA588"
			rewards: [{
				id: "6594B52599EFCB36"
				type: "xp"
				xp: 10
			}]
			subtitle: "Farming becomes cooking, hospitality and settlement design"
			tasks: [{
				id: "08523CD051A3118F"
				title: "I read this field note and tested the idea"
				type: "checkmark"
			}]
			title: "The Hearth Layer"
			x: 2.0d
			y: 0.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["20245EF322046A0F"]
			description: [
				"Create is the main technology mod. Shafts move rotation, cogs change layout, gearboxes redirect it, belts move items, and machines consume stress capacity rather than electrical power."
				"Central Kitchen and Slice and Dice connect Create to food; Enchantment Industry handles experience and enchantments; Steam 'n' Rails expands trains; Copycats, Connected and Deco make machinery fit a build."
				"Build one process at a time and leave space around it. A machine that can be explained, stopped and repaired by a friend is more advanced than a faster machine nobody understands."
				"The index separates world generation, homesteading, engineering, creatures, treasure, and optimisation so a new player can choose a direction without reading hundreds of pages in order."
			]
			id: "0762C4053BFAD78C"
			rewards: [{
				id: "33C3C905B97648D4"
				type: "xp"
				xp: 10
			}]
			subtitle: "Create turns motion into visible, understandable automation"
			tasks: [{
				id: "5388F8737F324232"
				title: "I read this field note and tested the idea"
				type: "checkmark"
			}]
			title: "The Engineering Layer"
			x: 2.0d
			y: 2.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["237EC65649665A03"]
			description: [
				"The Twilight Forest uses advancement-gated boss progression. The Aether restarts material progression in floating islands and three dungeon tiers. Deeper and Darker makes the Warden the key to the Otherside."
				"Alex's Caves hides six rare cave biomes behind tablets, a compendium and cave maps. Aquamirae places a frozen Ice Maze and drowned Ship Graveyard into cold oceans."
				"Do not enter these as ordinary mining trips. Read their chapter, establish a return point and decide what would make the expedition complete before crossing the threshold."
				"Library, compatibility, and performance mods may appear in the installed list without their own adventure chapter. They support the experience; they are not missing content that players need to craft or conquer."
			]
			id: "4287525D5D13FC1B"
			rewards: [{
				id: "24E6CECD719BCFD1"
				type: "xp"
				xp: 10
			}]
			subtitle: "Each major destination has its own rules"
			tasks: [{
				id: "37EF1D81F7B19718"
				title: "I read this field note and tested the idea"
				type: "checkmark"
			}]
			title: "The Adventure Layer"
			x: 4.0d
			y: -2.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["25171C2FD0FDA588", "4287525D5D13FC1B"]
			description: [
				"Alex's Mobs, Naturalist, Critters and Companions, Friends and Foes, biome mob overhauls and aquatic mods make ecosystems more varied. Many creatures are neutral, territorial, tameable or useful without being killed."
				"Doggy Talents Next and Domestication Innovation turn pets into long-term companions with needs, modes and equipment. Mowzie's Mobs adds encounter-driven creatures whose animations teach their combat rules."
				"Identify first, watch second and interact third. The pack rewards a field naturalist more often than it rewards someone swinging at every unfamiliar silhouette."
				"The index separates world generation, homesteading, engineering, creatures, treasure, and optimisation so a new player can choose a direction without reading hundreds of pages in order."
			]
			id: "652F7ADFB3FFC029"
			rewards: [{
				id: "285060F139B7D8D5"
				type: "xp"
				xp: 10
			}]
			subtitle: "Animals, companions and bosses are not interchangeable mobs"
			tasks: [{
				id: "1960A784E768B36A"
				title: "I read this field note and tested the idea"
				type: "checkmark"
			}]
			title: "The Creature Layer"
			x: 4.0d
			y: 0.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["25171C2FD0FDA588"]
			description: [
				"Lootr gives supported chests an individual inventory for each player. Artifacts adds curios found through exploration and mimics, while Relics gives unusual equipment a research and progression system."
				"Better Archeology adds suspicious blocks, fossils, artifact shards and an analysis table. Display mods, labels, photographs and albums turn isolated finds into a public record."
				"Before salvaging or equipping something rare, identify its mod with Jade or the tooltip, read its uses in JEI and ask whether it belongs in a loadout, workshop or museum."
				"The index separates world generation, homesteading, engineering, creatures, treasure, and optimisation so a new player can choose a direction without reading hundreds of pages in order."
			]
			id: "5D8FE8F2CB87C6DA"
			rewards: [{
