		{
			dependencies: ["652F7ADFB3FFC029", "78EB0B22EC380E61"]
			description: [
				"If you want a home, follow Homestead. If you want machines, follow Create. If you want a destination, choose one dimension or the structure chapter. If you want collecting, begin with wildlife, archaeology or photography."
				"Do not attempt every chapter at once. Bring one branch to a satisfying milestone, then let what you discovered suggest the next branch."
				"The guide is flexible because the server is a shared world, not a solo campaign with one correct build order. Your path can cross your friends' paths without replacing them."
				"The index separates world generation, homesteading, engineering, creatures, treasure, and optimisation so a new player can choose a direction without reading hundreds of pages in order."
			]
			id: "33454B8363C2C12A"
			rewards: [{
				id: "26D7153B11C6C5CD"
				type: "xp"
				xp: 10
			}]
			subtitle: "A beginner only needs one next question"
			tasks: [{
				id: "4899FDEB334FA275"
				title: "I read this field note and tested the idea"
				type: "checkmark"
			}]
			title: "Choose One Thread"
			x: 6.0d
			y: 1.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["33454B8363C2C12A"]
			description: [
				"When a mod surprises you, record the useful part: the block name, creature behaviour, structure entrance, machine failure or recipe category that finally made sense."
				"Put that knowledge into signs, books, maps, albums and builds. A quest book can introduce the world, but only the players can keep its field notes alive."
				"In the Chronicle, knowledge becomes a horizon when it is shared. Mark this complete when you have chosen your first thread and told the group what you hope to learn."
				"Use this index to decide which chapter answers the current question. Recipe viewers explain inputs, guidebooks explain a single mod, and the Field Guide connects those facts to this server's shared progression."
			]
			id: "6372F0702CB1687B"
			rewards: [{
				id: "4FAAA726961A969E"
				type: "xp"
				xp: 20
			}]
			subtitle: "Learn enough to leave useful clues for the next explorer"
